 statement that implies the printed one. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.lem-half-divisor-unit-drop"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.lem-half-divisor-unit-drop"],"id":"long.lem-half-divisor-unit-drop","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Lemma 6.51 (The effect of adding one divisor)","locator":"Long record Lemma 6.51, p. 58, label lem:half-divisor-unit-drop","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $N\\ge0$ and let finite supports $D_0,D_1$ differ only by $D_1=D_0\\cup\\{N+1\\}$, with $N+1\\notin D_0$. For every positive integer $m$,\n$$\nc_{D_1}(m)-c_{D_0}(m)=\\mathbf1_{N+1\\mid m}.\n$$\nIn particular, the difference is $1$ at $m=2(N+1)$. This follows directly from the definition of a divisor count. Its use in another coefficient sequence requires proving that sequence has the same support-incidence description.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.lem-half-divisor-unit-drop","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.lem-half-divisor-unit-drop","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.lem-half-divisor-unit-drop%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfCylinderIntegerGreedy.supportCoeff_insert_eq_add_indicator%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.lem-half-divisor-unit-drop%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfCylinderIntegerGreedy.supportCoeff_insert_eq_add_indicator%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.HalfCylinderIntegerGreedy.supportCoeff_insert_eq_add_indicator"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de7928